\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces What the primary experiment could have found, and how often it could have confirmed it. \emph  {(a)} Cumulative number of independent systems whose best fine-channel window reaches a given $P_{90}$, the power recovered in 90 per cent of injection trials. The thresholds span $6.3\times 10^{13}$ to $2.0\times 10^{16}$\,W, median $1.3\times 10^{15}$\,W, so a single quoted sensitivity would describe almost none of the survey; 19{} systems lie within a decade of the deepest. \emph  {(b)} Independent execution blocks per system. 27{} of the 82{} systems have only one --- and restricted to the primary experiment, 42{} of the 60{} Class\nobreakspace  {}A systems have more than one block, 70{} per cent --- so for the rest the recurrence test that defines a confirmed technosignature cannot be applied at all; 67{} per cent have two or more.}}{16}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:classasens}{{6}{16}{What the primary experiment could have found, and how often it could have confirmed it. \emph {(a)} Cumulative number of independent systems whose best fine-channel window reaches a given $P_{90}$, the power recovered in 90 per cent of injection trials. The thresholds span $\PNinetySysBestA $ to $\PNinetySysWorstA $\,W, median $\PNinetySysMedA $\,W, so a single quoted sensitivity would describe almost none of the survey; \ClassASysDecade {} systems lie within a decade of the deepest. \emph {(b)} Independent execution blocks per system. \NSysOneEB {} of the \NSystems {} systems have only one --- and restricted to the primary experiment, \NSysClassAMulti {} of the \NSysClassA {} Class~A systems have more than one block, \PctSysClassAMulti {} per cent --- so for the rest the recurrence test that defines a confirmed technosignature cannot be applied at all; \PctSysMultiEB {} per cent have two or more}{figure.6}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces The chance expectations quoted in this paper, and what each one assumes. They differ because each is conditioned differently, and the paper quotes two of them deliberately: the all-window figure, because every searched window was screened and so was eligible \emph  {a priori}, and the Class\nobreakspace  {}A figure, because every stage-1 outlier is in fact Class\nobreakspace  {}A. The last row is the narrow reference class and is the one that creates the tension reported in \S  \ref  {sec:technosearch}.}}{17}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:chance}{{8}{17}{The chance expectations quoted in this paper, and what each one assumes. They differ because each is conditioned differently, and the paper quotes two of them deliberately: the all-window figure, because every searched window was screened and so was eligible \emph {a priori}, and the Class~A figure, because every stage-1 outlier is in fact Class~A. The last row is the narrow reference class and is the one that creates the tension reported in \S \ref {sec:technosearch}}{table.8}{}}
