\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces The CP$-$72\nobreakspace  {}2713 repeat test in full, both blocks side by side, so the reader can tell ``not detected again'' from ``a persistent signal of the original strength would have been recovered''. The repeat block is the deeper of the two, matches the first in tuning, channelisation and integration, and its frequency axis registers to a fifth of a channel. A source at the first block's flux would have returned $T_\star =6.21$ there; the measured value is 4.70. Intermittent emission is not excluded by this test, and no statement here assumes otherwise.}}{24}{table.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:cprepeat}{{14}{24}{The CP$-$72~2713 repeat test in full, both blocks side by side, so the reader can tell ``not detected again'' from ``a persistent signal of the original strength would have been recovered''. The repeat block is the deeper of the two, matches the first in tuning, channelisation and integration, and its frequency axis registers to a fifth of a channel. A source at the first block's flux would have returned $T_\star =\CpRecExpT $ there; the measured value is \CpTstarTwo . Intermittent emission is not excluded by this test, and no statement here assumes otherwise}{table.14}{}}
